  <!--
    HOW THIS FEED WORKS (read me before editing):

    Subscribers are pinged ONCE per <item>, keyed by its <guid>. This feed is
    hand-maintained and separate from your post HTML, so editing/tweaking a post
    NEVER pings anyone. You get pinged out only when YOU add a new <item> here.

    This file is now auto-synced from blog.html's post list by
    scripts/generate_feed.py, run on every push via
    .github/workflows/feed.yml. Existing <item> blocks are matched by <guid>
    and left untouched; only a post in blog.html with no matching guid yet
    gets a new <item> appended (with a naive auto-generated description you
    can hand-edit afterwards, safely, since guid is what's permanent).
    You can still add an <item> by hand instead; the script will leave it
    alone once its guid exists.

    To announce something by hand instead of waiting on the automation:
      1. Copy the template block below.
      2. Paste it directly under this comment (newest item on top).
      3. Fill in title, link, description, and pubDate.
      4. Give it a NEW, permanent <guid> (never reuse or change one).
      5. Commit + push. That's the "send" button.

    pubDate must be RFC-822, e.g.  Mon, 22 Jun 2026 12:00:00 +0000
    Get today's:  date -u '+%a, %d %b %Y %H:%M:%S +0000'

    TEMPLATE (leave commented; copy it, don't edit it in place):
    <item>
      <title>Post title here</title>
      <link>https://sashacarin.github.io/posts/slug.html</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">sashaslib-UNIQUE-ID</guid>
      <description>One-line summary.</description>
      <pubDate>Mon, 22 Jun 2026 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    </item>
  -->

